				<!-- wp:villacde-core/reviews-carousel -->
				<div class="wp-block-villacde-core-reviews-carousel villacde-reviews-carousel"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="44" height="34" viewBox="0 0 44 34" fill="#E8913A" class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote-icon"><path d="M0 34V20C0 8 6 1 18 0v7c-6 1-9 5-9 11h9v16zM26 34V20C26 8 32 1 44 0v7c-6 1-9 5-9 11h9v16z"></path></svg><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__track"><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review"><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">Six bedrooms meant nobody had to share and every en-suite was spotless, but the thing we still talk about is the chef. We handed over a shopping list on Friday evening and did not think about food again until Sunday night.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Wanjiru M.</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · Nairobi · September 2026</span></p></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review" hidden><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">We booked it for the pool and barely left the water. The children were swimming by nine each morning, and in the evening the staff lit the fire pit without being asked. Longonot turns pink at about half six. Bring a jumper, it gets properly cold after dark.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Daniel O.</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · Nakuru · August 2026</span></p></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review" hidden><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">We held my mother's sixtieth here with fourteen of us. The lawn took a marquee easily, the house manager helped us carry the dining table outside, and the gate staff looked after guests who arrived late. It did not feel like a rental. It felt like a house someone lends you.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Faith K.</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · Nairobi · July 2026</span></p></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review" hidden><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">Two people in a six-bedroom villa is excessive and we would do it again tomorrow. Coffee on the rooftop with Mount Longonot straight ahead, no traffic, no neighbours, nothing to do. We kept the lounge fire going both nights.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Peter &amp; Alice N.</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · Mombasa · June 2026</span></p></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review" hidden><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">Two hours from Westlands, door to gate, tarmac nearly the whole way. Gated estate, a guard at the entrance and parking inside for four cars, so we stopped worrying about the vehicles within ten minutes of arriving.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Samuel Githinji</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · Nairobi · October 2026</span></p></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__review" hidden><blockquote class="villacde-reviews-carousel__quote">We used the villa as a base for Hell's Gate and a boat ride on the lake, both under twenty minutes away, then came back to the pool each afternoon. The small round pool is lit blue at night and my daughters decided that was the best part of Kenya.</blockquote><p class="villacde-reviews-carousel__byline"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__name">Rebecca T.</span><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__meta"> · London, UK · August 2026</span></p></div></div><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__footer"><span class="villacde-reviews-carousel__count">1 / 6</span><div class="villacde-reviews-carousel__nav"><button type="button" class="villacde-reviews-carousel__btn villacde-reviews-carousel__btn--prev" aria-label="Previous review" data-rv="pre